## 2. File Layout

```
{{project-name}}/
├── index.html          ← entry point
├── game.mjs            ← main game loop + state machine
├── player.mjs          ← player controller
├── enemies.mjs         ← enemy spawner + AI
├── scenes.mjs          ← level/scene definitions
├── audio.mjs           ← Web Audio API wrapper
├── juice.mjs           ← screen shake, particles, hit-stop
├── analytics.mjs       ← telemetry event dispatcher
├── assets/
│   ├── sprites/        ← PNG/SVG assets
│   ├── audio/          ← OGG/MP3 SFX + music
│   └── fonts/          ← web fonts (if any)
└── CREDITS.md          ← asset attribution
```

## 3. Module Responsibilities

| Module | Owns | Calls | Called by |
|--------|------|-------|----------|
| `game.mjs` | State machine, game loop, delta time | all modules | `index.html` |
| `player.mjs` | Player state, input handling | — | `game.mjs` |
| `enemies.mjs` | Enemy pool, spawn logic, AI | — | `game.mjs` |
| `scenes.mjs` | Level data, progression gates | — | `game.mjs` |
| `audio.mjs` | AudioContext, SFX playback | — | `game.mjs`, `player.mjs` |

## 4. State Machine

States: `title` → `playing` → `paused` → `game_over(win|lose)` → `title`

Refer to `screen_flow_v1` for full transition table.

## 5. Input Model

{{Reference screen_flow_v1 input bindings. Specify implementation:}}
- Keyboard: `keydown`/`keyup` with key state map (no per-frame event checks)
- Touch: `pointerdown`/`pointermove`/`pointerup` for unified mouse+touch
- Gamepad: `navigator.getGamepads()` polled per frame (if applicable)

## 6. Asset Loader Strategy

| Asset type | Loading | Cache |
|-----------|---------|-------|
| Sprites | `fetch()` + `createImageBitmap()` on init | In-memory Map |
| Audio | `fetch()` + `decodeAudioData()` on init | AudioBuffer Map |
| Fonts | `<link rel="preload">` in `<head>` | Browser cache |

All paths relative. No CDN. Must work from `file://`.

## 7. Performance Budget

| Metric | Target | Measurement |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| First playable | < 3s on 50Mbps | Playwright `load` → first `requestAnimationFrame` |
| Frame rate | 60fps (16.6ms budget) | `performance.now()` delta in game loop |
| Total assets | < 5MB | `du -sh assets/` |
| JS bundle | < 500KB gzipped | `gzip -c *.mjs | wc -c` |
| Memory | < 256MB heap | DevTools Memory panel |

## 8. Test Hook

```javascript
window.__game = {
  player: { x, y, hp, score, state },
  enemies: [{ x, y, hp, type }],
  projectiles: [{ x, y, dx, dy, owner }],
  state: "title" | "playing" | "paused" | "win" | "lose"
}
```

## 9. Coding Standards

- `requestAnimationFrame` for game loop (not `setInterval`)
- `performance.now()` for delta time (not `Date.now()`)
- No global state pollution — namespace under `window.__game`
- No `eval()`, `new Function()`, `innerHTML` with user data
- Max cyclomatic complexity: 10. Max function length: 40 lines.

